    {
      "id": "516fa0d9-3a7d-4d8f-8f76-8bbf3bdb3319",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Array – properties\r\n\r\nAn array stores a **fixed number** of values of the **same type** in one variable.\r\n\r\n**Properties**\r\n- Size is fixed when the array is created; it cannot grow or shrink.\r\n- Every item has an **index** starting at `0`: `names[0]` is the first item.\r\n- `names.length` gives the number of items (a property, no brackets).\r\n- Can store primitives (`int`, `double`, `char`…) as well as objects (`String`…).\r\n- Reading an index that does not exist throws `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException`.\r\n- Need a list that can grow? Use `ArrayList`, `List` or `Vector` (below).",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "516fa0d9-3a7d-4d8f-8f76-8bbf3bdb3319"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bf1b4128-f60a-4e90-b822-c11c701ac753",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "//Syntax\r\n//data_type [] variable_name = value;\r\n\r\n\r\n// Method: type[] name = {values}\r\n// What:   creates an array; its size is fixed by the number of values (here 3)\r\n// Use:    to store a fixed number of values of the same type\r\nString[] names = {\"Zoya\", \"Jane\", \"Doe\"};\r\n// Method: name[index]  (not a method, index access)\r\n// What:   reads the item at the index; the first item is at index 0\r\n// Use:    to get one value out of the array\r\nSystem.out.println(\"The first name is: \" + names[0]); // Output: The first name is: John",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "bf1b4128-f60a-4e90-b822-c11c701ac753",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 3,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 3,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "The first name is: Zoya\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "a77e0273-f7e0-423a-8c91-7525e2e7626f",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# ArrayList – properties and methods\r\n\r\n`ArrayList` is a **resizable array** from the `java.util` package.\r\n\r\n**Properties**\r\n- Size is not fixed: it grows automatically when you add items (a normal array cannot grow).\r\n- Keeps the **insertion order** and every item has an **index** starting at `0`.\r\n- Allows **duplicate** values and `null`.\r\n- Can only store **objects**, so use `Integer`, `Double`, `Character`… instead of `int`, `double`, `char`.\r\n- Default capacity is **10**; when it is full it grows by about **50%**.\r\n- **Not synchronized** (not thread-safe), which makes it faster than `Vector`.\r\n- Fast `get(index)`; slower to add/remove in the middle because items have to shift.",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "a77e0273-f7e0-423a-8c91-7525e2e7626f"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3facb902-799b-468d-aeb7-ab2cb613d8d0",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "//Syntax\r\n//ArrayList<DataType> variable_name = new ArrayList<DataType>();\r\n\r\n//this is to create an empty ArrayList\r\nArrayList<String> fruits = new ArrayList<String>();\r\nSystem.out.println(\"The list is: \" + fruits);\r\n// Method: size()\r\n// What:   returns how many items are in the list\r\n// Use:    to know the length, e.g. for the last index: size() - 1\r\nSystem.out.println(\"The size is: \" + fruits.size());\r\n\r\n//this is to create an ArrayList with a starting capacity of 20\r\nArrayList<Integer> marks = new ArrayList<>(20);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"The marks list is: \" + marks);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "3facb902-799b-468d-aeb7-ab2cb613d8d0",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 26,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 26,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "The list is: []\r\nThe size is: 0\r\nThe marks list is: []\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 26
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "5a176b6b-cc06-4089-8c50-b7b258e79844",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "ArrayList<String> fruits = new ArrayList<String>();\r\n\r\n//this is to add items at the end of the list\r\n// Method: add(item) / add(index, item)\r\n// What:   adds an item at the end, or inserts it at the given index (items after it shift right)\r\n// Use:    to put new values into the list\r\nfruits.add(\"Apple\");\r\nfruits.add(\"Banana\");\r\nfruits.add(\"Mango\");\r\nfruits.add(\"Orange\");\r\nfruits.add(\"Banana\"); // duplicates are allowed\r\n\r\nSystem.out.println(\"The list is: \" + fruits);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "5a176b6b-cc06-4089-8c50-b7b258e79844",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 27,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 27,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "The list is: [Apple, Banana, Mango, Orange, Banana]\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 27
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "8cf2c94b-5b44-49e7-8743-19f0eca8b0c7",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "    //Syntax\r\n\r\n    //DataTypeList<DataType> variable_name = new DataTypeList<DataType>();\r\n\r\n    ArrayList<String> namesList = new ArrayList<String>();\r\n    // Method: add(item) / add(index, item)\r\n    // What:   adds an item at the end, or inserts it at the given index (items after it shift right)\r\n    // Use:    to put new values into the list\r\n    namesList.add(\"Prachi\");\r\n    namesList.add(\"Krishita\");\r\n    namesList.add(\"Zoya\");\r\n\r\n    // Method: addAll(collection) / addAll(index, collection)\r\n    // What:   adds every item of another collection at the end, or at the given index\r\n    // Use:    to add many values in one step instead of calling add() again and again\r\n    namesList.addAll(Arrays.asList(\"surbhi\",\"humaira\",\"Gayatri\",\"pratik\"));\r\n\r\n    System.out.println(\"The list is: \" + namesList); // Output: The list is: [Prachi, Krishita, Zoya, surbhi, humaira, Gayatri, pratik]\r\n\r\n    //this is to verify contains method\r\n    // Method: contains(item)\r\n    // What:   returns true if the item is in the list\r\n    // Use:    to check if a value exists before using it\r\n    boolean is_exist = namesList.contains(\"Zoya\");\r\n    System.out.println(\"Is Zoya in the list? : \" + is_exist);\r\n\r\n    //this is to verify contains method \r\n    boolean is_exist = namesList.contains(\"arbaz\");\r\n    System.out.println(\"Is arbaz in the list? : \" + is_exist);\r\n\r\n    // this is to verify contains all method     \r\n    // Method: containsAll(collection)\r\n    // What:   returns true only if EVERY item of the other collection is in the list\r\n    // Use:    to check many values at once\r\n    boolean is_exist = namesList.containsAll(Arrays.asList(\"Zoya\", \"Krishita\"));\r\n    System.out.println(\"Are Zoya and Krishita in the list? : \" + is_exist);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "8cf2c94b-5b44-49e7-8743-19f0eca8b0c7",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 11,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 11,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "The list is: [Prachi, Krishita, Zoya, surbhi, humaira, Gayatri, pratik]\r\nIs Zoya in the list? : true\r\nIs arbaz in the list? : false\r\nAre Zoya and Krishita in the list? : true\r\nThe list is: [Prachi, Krishita, Zoya, surbhi, humaira, Gayatri, pratik]\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 11
        }
      ]
