    {
      "id": "99036402-51ce-472e-a76a-c22624da59f7",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "ArrayList<String> namesList = new ArrayList<String>();\r\n\r\n// Method: add(item) / add(index, item)\r\n// What:   adds an item at the end, or inserts it at the given index (items after it shift right)\r\n// Use:    to put new values into the list\r\nnamesList.add(\"Prachi\");\r\nnamesList.add(\"Krishita\");\r\nnamesList.add(\"Zoya\");\r\n\r\n// Method: addAll(collection) / addAll(index, collection)\r\n// What:   adds every item of another collection at the end, or at the given index\r\n// Use:    to add many values in one step instead of calling add() again and again\r\nnamesList.addAll(Arrays.asList(\"surbhi\",\"humaira\",\"Gayatri\",\"pratik\"));\r\n\r\nSystem.out.println(\"The list is: \" + namesList);\r\n\r\n//this is to clear the list\r\n// Method: clear()\r\n// What:   removes every item; the list becomes empty but can still be used\r\n// Use:    to reset the list and start again\r\nnamesList.clear();\r\n// Method: isEmpty()\r\n// What:   returns true if the list has no items\r\n// Use:    to check before reading so you do not get an error\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Is the list cleared? : \" + namesList.isEmpty());\r\nnamesList.\r\nSystem.out.println(\"The list is: \" + namesList); // Output: The list is: []\r\n// System.out.println(\"The list is: \" + namesList); // Output: The list is: []",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "99036402-51ce-472e-a76a-c22624da59f7",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 14,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 14,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "The list is: [Prachi, Krishita, Zoya, surbhi, humaira, Gayatri, pratik]\r\nIs the list cleared? : true\r\nThe list is: []\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 14
        }
