    {
      "id": "d3bfedac-4680-469c-b03c-77fb961a412f",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "ArrayList<String> fruits = new ArrayList<>(List.of(\"Apple\", \"Banana\", \"Mango\"));\r\n\r\n//this is to add an item at a given index (the others shift to the right)\r\n// Method: add(item) / add(index, item)\r\n// What:   adds an item at the end, or inserts it at the given index (items after it shift right)\r\n// Use:    to put new values into the list\r\nfruits.add(1, \"Grapes\");\r\nSystem.out.println(\"The list is: \" + fruits);",
      "metadata": {
