    {
      "id": "2a926366-0dda-445d-a889-68c3dc9582bc",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "ArrayList<String> fruits = new ArrayList<>(List.of(\"Apple\", \"Banana\", \"Mango\"));\r\n\r\n//this is to convert the ArrayList into a normal array\r\n// Method: toArray(new Type[0])\r\n// What:   copies the items into a normal array\r\n// Use:    when a method needs an array instead of a list\r\nString[] fruitArray = fruits.toArray(new String[0]);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Array length: \" + fruitArray.length);\r\n// Method: Arrays.toString(array)\r\n// What:   turns an array into readable text like [a, b, c]\r\n// Use:    to print an array (println(array) prints only a memory address)\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Array: \" + Arrays.toString(fruitArray));",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "2a926366-0dda-445d-a889-68c3dc9582bc",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 41,
