      "execution_count": 47,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "Before clear: [Apple, Banana, Mango]\r\nAfter clear: []\r\nIs the list empty? : true\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 47
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "6da4543e-d446-4244-ae21-757c0991cbd7",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# List – properties and methods\r\n\r\n`List` is an **interface**, not a class. It describes what an ordered collection can do. You cannot write `new List<>()`; you create one of its implementations instead:\r\n\r\n| Implementation | Good for |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `ArrayList` | Fast reading by index (most common choice) |\r\n| `Vector` | Thread-safe (older class) |\r\n\r\n**Properties**\r\n- Ordered, index-based (starts at `0`), allows duplicates and `null` (except `List.of`).\r\n- Writing `List<String> x = new ArrayList<>();` is called *programming to the interface*: you can later switch to `Vector` (or another `List`) by changing only the right side.\r\n- Shortcut ways to create a list:\r\n  - `List.of(...)` → **immutable** (cannot add, remove or set; trying it stops the program with an error).\r\n  - `Arrays.asList(...)` → **fixed size** (can `set`, cannot `add`/`remove`).\r\n  - `List.copyOf(list)` → immutable copy.",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "6da4543e-d446-4244-ae21-757c0991cbd7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "9825191a-e640-401a-8202-aecaf0727fc9",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "//Syntax\r\n//List<DataType> variable_name = new ArrayList<DataType>();\r\n\r\n//this is to create a List using ArrayList and add items\r\nList<String> cities = new ArrayList<String>();\r\n// Method: add(item) / add(index, item)\r\n// What:   adds an item at the end, or inserts it at the given index (items after it shift right)\r\n// Use:    to put new values into the list\r\ncities.add(\"Mumbai\");\r\ncities.add(\"Delhi\");\r\ncities.add(\"Pune\");\r\n\r\nSystem.out.println(\"The list is: \" + cities);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "9825191a-e640-401a-8202-aecaf0727fc9",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 48,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 48,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "The list is: [Mumbai, Delhi, Pune]\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 48
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "6473e49e-e3a5-4353-b2c9-6a00de4281bf",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "List<String> nameList = new ArrayList<String>();\r\n// Method: add(item) / add(index, item)\r\n// What:   adds an item at the end, or inserts it at the given index (items after it shift right)\r\n// Use:    to put new values into the list\r\nnameList.add(\"Prachi\");\r\nnameList.add(\"Krishita\");\r\nnameList.add(\"Zoya\");\r\n\r\n// Method: indexOf(item) / indexOf(item, fromIndex)\r\n// What:   returns the index of the first match, or -1 if not found\r\n// Use:    to find where a value is in the list\r\nint index = nameList.indexOf(\"Krishita\");\r\nSystem.out.println(\"The index of 'Krishita' is: \" + index);\r\n\r\nSystem.out.println(\"The list is: \" + nameList);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "6473e49e-e3a5-4353-b2c9-6a00de4281bf",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 23,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 23,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "The index of 'Krishita' is: 1\r\nThe list is: [Prachi, Krishita, Zoya]\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 23
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0e9589cb-9bff-47a7-b252-f742fabfc443",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "//this is to create an IMMUTABLE list with List.of()\r\n// Method: List.of(items...)\r\n// What:   creates an IMMUTABLE list (cannot add, remove or set)\r\n// Use:    for fixed data that must not change\r\nList<String> cities = List.of(\"Mumbai\", \"Delhi\", \"Pune\");\r\nSystem.out.println(\"The list is: \" + cities);\r\n\r\n//cities.add(\"Goa\");   // not allowed: a List.of() list cannot be changed (the program stops with an error)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "0e9589cb-9bff-47a7-b252-f742fabfc443",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 50,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 50,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "The list is: [Mumbai, Delhi, Pune]\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 50
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0f5d1f3e-04b1-415c-addc-8fb21f2dd042",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "//this is to create a FIXED-SIZE list from values with Arrays.asList()\r\n// Method: Arrays.asList(items...)\r\n// What:   creates a FIXED-SIZE list backed by an array (set() works, add()/remove() do not)\r\n// Use:    to quickly turn values or an array into a List\r\nList<String> cities = Arrays.asList(\"Mumbai\", \"Delhi\", \"Pune\");\r\n\r\n//set() is allowed\r\n// Method: set(index, item)\r\n// What:   replaces the item at the given index and returns the old value\r\n// Use:    to update a value that is already in the list\r\ncities.set(0, \"Chennai\");\r\nSystem.out.println(\"After set: \" + cities);\r\n\r\n//cities.add(\"Goa\");   // not allowed: the size of an Arrays.asList() list is fixed (the program stops with an error)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "0f5d1f3e-04b1-415c-addc-8fb21f2dd042",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 51,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 51,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "After set: [Chennai, Delhi, Pune]\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 51
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "46962d6c-69b8-4fc6-9c45-16f7223b59c5",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "List<String> cities = new ArrayList<>(List.of(\"Mumbai\", \"Delhi\"));\r\n\r\n//this is to make an immutable copy; later changes to the original do not affect it\r\n// Method: List.copyOf(list)\r\n// What:   makes an IMMUTABLE copy of a list\r\n// Use:    to keep a snapshot that later changes cannot affect\r\nList<String> snapshot = List.copyOf(cities);\r\n// Method: add(item) / add(index, item)\r\n// What:   adds an item at the end, or inserts it at the given index (items after it shift right)\r\n// Use:    to put new values into the list\r\ncities.add(\"Pune\");\r\n\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Original: \" + cities);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Copy: \" + snapshot);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "46962d6c-69b8-4fc6-9c45-16f7223b59c5",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 52,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 52,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "Original: [Mumbai, Delhi, Pune]\r\nCopy: [Mumbai, Delhi]\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 52
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "73cd2524-ebf6-49e9-99fc-feb33fb54636",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "List<String> cities = new ArrayList<>(List.of(\"Mumbai\", \"Delhi\", \"Pune\"));\r\n\r\n//this is to read and replace items by index\r\n// Method: get(index)\r\n// What:   returns the item at the given index (index starts at 0)\r\n// Use:    to read one value from the list\r\nSystem.out.println(\"City at index 1: \" + cities.get(1));\r\n// Method: set(index, item)\r\n// What:   replaces the item at the given index and returns the old value\r\n// Use:    to update a value that is already in the list\r\ncities.set(1, \"Kolkata\");\r\nSystem.out.println(\"After set: \" + cities);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "73cd2524-ebf6-49e9-99fc-feb33fb54636",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 53,
          "success": true
