    {
      "id": "32ced240-21bd-4e05-ac3e-85c6fd2571cc",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Vector<String> colors = new Vector<>(List.of(\"Red\", \"Green\", \"Blue\", \"Green\"));\r\n\r\n//this is to search the vector\r\n// Method: contains(item)\r\n// What:   returns true if the item is in the list\r\n// Use:    to check if a value exists before using it\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Contains Blue? : \" + colors.contains(\"Blue\"));\r\n// Method: indexOf(item) / indexOf(item, fromIndex)\r\n// What:   returns the index of the first match, or -1 if not found\r\n// Use:    to find where a value is in the list\r\nSystem.out.println(\"First index of Green: \" + colors.indexOf(\"Green\"));\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Index of Green searching from index 2: \" + colors.indexOf(\"Green\", 2));\r\n// Method: lastIndexOf(item)\r\n// What:   returns the index of the last match, or -1 if not found\r\n// Use:    to find the last position of a value that appears more than once\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Last index of Green: \" + colors.lastIndexOf(\"Green\"));\r\n// Method: isEmpty()\r\n// What:   returns true if the list has no items\r\n// Use:    to check before reading so you do not get an error\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Is empty? : \" + colors.isEmpty());",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "32ced240-21bd-4e05-ac3e-85c6fd2571cc",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 71,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 71,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "Contains Blue? : true\r\nFirst index of Green: 1\r\nIndex of Green searching from index 2: 3\r\nLast index of Green: 3\r\nIs empty? : false\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 71
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "42bf3b9a-5e3d-4541-b0df-685e12d7b862",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Vector<String> colors = new Vector<>(List.of(\"Red\", \"Green\"));\r\n\r\n//this is to make room for at least 50 items\r\n// Method: ensureCapacity(n)\r\n// What:   makes sure there is room for at least n items\r\n// Use:    to avoid many slow resizes when you know many items are coming\r\ncolors.ensureCapacity(50);\r\n// Method: capacity()  [Vector only]\r\n// What:   returns how many items fit before the Vector has to grow (not the same as size())\r\n// Use:    to see how the internal storage grows\r\nSystem.out.println(\"After ensureCapacity(50): Capacity = \" + colors.capacity());\r\n\r\n//this is to shrink the capacity to the current size\r\n// Method: trimToSize()\r\n// What:   shrinks the capacity down to the current size\r\n// Use:    to free unused memory after you finish adding\r\ncolors.trimToSize();\r\nSystem.out.println(\"After trimToSize(): Capacity = \" + colors.capacity());",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "42bf3b9a-5e3d-4541-b0df-685e12d7b862",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 73,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 73,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "After ensureCapacity(50): Capacity = 50\r\nAfter trimToSize(): Capacity = 2\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 73
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fde90236-85a2-46dd-8c62-8bd25ea200ba",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Vector<String> colors = new Vector<>(List.of(\"Red\", \"Green\", \"Blue\", \"Yellow\"));\r\n\r\n//this is to change the size: bigger fills with null, smaller cuts off the end\r\n// Method: setSize(n)  [Vector only]\r\n// What:   changes the size: bigger fills new places with null, smaller cuts items off the end\r\n// Use:    to force the Vector to an exact size\r\ncolors.setSize(6);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"After setSize(6): \" + colors);\r\n\r\ncolors.setSize(2);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"After setSize(2): \" + colors);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "fde90236-85a2-46dd-8c62-8bd25ea200ba",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 74,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 74,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "After setSize(6): [Red, Green, Blue, Yellow, null, null]\r\nAfter setSize(2): [Red, Green]\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 74
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c8958e77-e586-429c-b00c-1c36c3157a47",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Vector<String> colors = new Vector<>(List.of(\"Red\", \"Green\", \"Blue\"));\r\n\r\n//this is to copy the items into an existing array (legacy)\r\n// Method: size()\r\n// What:   returns how many items are in the list\r\n// Use:    to know the length, e.g. for the last index: size() - 1\r\nString[] colorArray = new String[colors.size()];\r\n// Method: copyInto(array)  [Vector only, legacy]\r\n// What:   copies the items into an array you already created\r\n// Use:    in old Vector code; new code uses toArray()\r\ncolors.copyInto(colorArray);\r\n// Method: Arrays.toString(array)\r\n// What:   turns an array into readable text like [a, b, c]\r\n// Use:    to print an array (println(array) prints only a memory address)\r\nSystem.out.println(\"copyInto: \" + Arrays.toString(colorArray));\r\n\r\n//this is to convert to an array with toArray()\r\n// Method: toArray(new Type[0])\r\n// What:   copies the items into a normal array\r\n// Use:    when a method needs an array instead of a list\r\nSystem.out.println(\"toArray: \" + Arrays.toString(colors.toArray(new String[0])));",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "c8958e77-e586-429c-b00c-1c36c3157a47",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 75,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 75,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "copyInto: [Red, Green, Blue]\r\ntoArray: [Red, Green, Blue]\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 75
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cedfa711-caea-4f92-80e3-6264427c193a",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Vector<String> colors = new Vector<>(List.of(\"Yellow\", \"Red\", \"Blue\", \"Green\"));\r\n\r\n//this is to sort the vector in ascending (A to Z) order\r\n// Method: sort(null)\r\n// What:   sorts the list itself; null means natural order (A to Z, small to big)\r\n// Use:    to put the items in order\r\ncolors.sort(null);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Ascending: \" + colors);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "cedfa711-caea-4f92-80e3-6264427c193a",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 76,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 76,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "Ascending: [Blue, Green, Red, Yellow]\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 76
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "361108b4-5516-4fbc-a5aa-64efba88d813",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Vector<String> colors = new Vector<>(List.of(\"Red\", \"Green\"));\r\n\r\n//bulk methods work the same as ArrayList\r\n// Method: addAll(collection) / addAll(index, collection)\r\n// What:   adds every item of another collection at the end, or at the given index\r\n// Use:    to add many values in one step instead of calling add() again and again\r\ncolors.addAll(List.of(\"Blue\", \"Yellow\", \"Black\"));\r\nSystem.out.println(\"After addAll: \" + colors);\r\n\r\n// Method: removeAll(collection)\r\n// What:   removes every item that is also in the other collection\r\n// Use:    to delete many values in one step\r\ncolors.removeAll(List.of(\"Black\"));\r\nSystem.out.println(\"After removeAll: \" + colors);\r\n\r\n// Method: retainAll(collection)\r\n// What:   keeps ONLY the items that are also in the other collection; removes the rest\r\n// Use:    to find the common values between two lists\r\ncolors.retainAll(List.of(\"Red\", \"Blue\", \"Yellow\"));\r\nSystem.out.println(\"After retainAll: \" + colors);\r\n\r\n// Method: subList(fromIndex, toIndex)\r\n// What:   returns the part of the list from fromIndex (included) to toIndex (excluded)\r\n// Use:    to work with only a section of the list\r\nSystem.out.println(\"subList(0, 2): \" + colors.subList(0, 2));",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "361108b4-5516-4fbc-a5aa-64efba88d813",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 77,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 77,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "After addAll: [Red, Green, Blue, Yellow, Black]\r\nAfter removeAll: [Red, Green, Blue, Yellow]\r\nAfter retainAll: [Red, Blue, Yellow]\r\nsubList(0, 2): [Red, Blue]\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 77
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "e020785a-fed4-448f-8fb6-8082b5335de4",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Vector<String> colors = new Vector<>(List.of(\"Red\", \"Green\", \"Blue\"));\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Before: \" + colors);\r\n\r\n//this is to remove every item: removeAllElements() (legacy) and clear() do the same thing\r\n// Method: removeAllElements()  [Vector only, legacy]\r\n// What:   removes every item (same as clear())\r\n// Use:    in old Vector code; new code uses clear()\r\ncolors.removeAllElements();\r\n// Method: size()\r\n// What:   returns how many items are in the list\r\n// Use:    to know the length, e.g. for the last index: size() - 1\r\nSystem.out.println(\"After removeAllElements(): \" + colors + \" , size: \" + colors.size());",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "e020785a-fed4-448f-8fb6-8082b5335de4",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 78,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 78,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "Before: [Red, Green, Blue]\r\nAfter removeAllElements(): [] , size: 0\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 78
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c4647e36-a656-4c3c-8b67-a2e968bd0b27",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Array vs ArrayList vs List vs Vector\r\n\r\n| | Array (`String[]`) | `ArrayList` | `List` | `Vector` |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| What it is | Built-in language feature | Class | Interface | Class (legacy) |\r\n| Size | Fixed | Grows by ~50% | Depends on implementation | Grows ×2 (or by `capacityIncrement`) |\r\n| Stores primitives (`int`) | ✅ Yes | ❌ No, use `Integer` | ❌ No, use `Integer` | ❌ No, use `Integer` |\r\n| Length / size | `arr.length` | `list.size()` | `list.size()` | `vector.size()` |\r\n| Read item | `arr[i]` | `list.get(i)` | `list.get(i)` | `vector.get(i)` / `elementAt(i)` |\r\n| Thread-safe | ❌ | ❌ | Depends | ✅ Synchronized |\r\n| Speed | Fastest | Fast | Depends | Slower (locking) |\r\n| Use when | Size is known and fixed | Default choice for a list | Declaring variables and parameters | Maintaining old code |",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "c4647e36-a656-4c3c-8b67-a2e968bd0b27"
      }
    }
  ]
}